NNOOTTEESS
       This function had to be called "true gamma function" since there is
       already a function ggaammmmaa(3) that returns something else (see ggaammmmaa(3)
       for details).

BBUUGGSS
       Before glibc 2.18, the glibc implementation of these functions did not
       set _e_r_r_n_o to EEDDOOMM when _x is negative infinity.

       Before glibc 2.19, the glibc implementation of these functions did not
       set _e_r_r_n_o to EERRAANNGGEE on an underflow range error.

       In glibc versions 2.3.3 and earlier, an argument of +0 or -0
       incorrectly produced a domain error (_e_r_r_n_o set to EEDDOOMM and an
       FFEE__IINNVVAALLIIDD exception raised), rather than a pole error.

